                <p class="snippet" >
                     FC 218; Chemainus First Nation v. British Columbia Assets and Lands Corp., [1999] 3 C.N.L.R. 8; Gitanyow First Nation v. Canada, [1999] 3 C.N.L.R. 89; <b>Saadati v. Moorhead</b>, 2017 SCC 28, [2017] 1 S.C.R. 543; Shot Both Sides v. Canada, 2024 SCC 12; Clyde River (Hamlet) v. Petroleum Geo‐Services Inc., 2017 SCC 40, [2017] 1 &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;If Pekuakamiulnuatsh Takuhikan’s action were based solely on a civil fault, I would therefore find that the case should be remanded to the Superior Court so that it can determine the quantum of damages (Supreme Court Act, s. 46.1; <b>Saadati v. Moorhead</b>, 2017 SCC 28, [2017] 1 S.C.R. 543, at para. 45). [209] I turn now to the 
                </p>
